Subject: Keep build-machine Rust native when cross-building

Upstream-base: 0ff52079ca9e9e837ed27eb95a8d239f439a1864

MESA_SWITCH_RUST_TARGET lets an x86_64 host build NVK for the Switch, but the
wrapper also gave that target to procedural macros and their crates, which
rustc loads on the build machine. Apply it only to code linked with devkitA64.

--- a/rustc-switch-wrapper.sh
+++ b/rustc-switch-wrapper.sh
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@
     esac
 done
 
+# Only Switch code links with devkitA64. Procedural macros and the crates they
+# use run inside rustc on the build machine, so they keep its own target.
+case "$*" in
+    *aarch64-none-elf-*) ;;
+    *) RUST_TARGET= ;;
+esac
+
 if [ -n "$RUST_TARGET" ]; then
     exec "$RUSTC_BIN" --target="$RUST_TARGET" "$@"
 fi
